WEBVTT

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.320
Curious about how Canada's federal government reports using AI?

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:09.060
The AI Register makes the public record easier to explore, one system at a time.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:12.620
Choose Explore the register.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.760
Search for a topic, system name, or organisation.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.120
Let's try flood.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:20.220
The results match words in the information departments have supplied.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.060
Use Reported status to narrow the results.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:29.980
Select In production.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:35.400
More filters let you explore developers, vendors, notification and reported

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.200
status year.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.500
Open Flood Susceptibility Index.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.960
The dossier gathers the department's description, users, data sources and

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:44.560
reported results.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.700
A field marked Not specified means the information wasn't supplied.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.700
It doesn't mean the answer is no.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.740
Check the source record ID and the two dates.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:05.800
One describes the source dataset; the other identifies this explorer's snapshot.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.560
Official source opens the government dataset.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.940
Reported results are not independently verified outcomes.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.860
Close the record and reset the filters.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:23.140
Choose Patterns to compare reported statuses, organisations and other fields.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.420
Every chart has a data table.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:28.640
Select a category to see the records behind its count.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.460
Back in Records, you can sort or group the results.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:45.140
Export CSV downloads the complete filtered set, including records beyond the

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:45.820
first page.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:52.120
Switch between English and French, or choose a darker theme.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.020
Start with a question.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:55.100
Explore the records.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:57.620
Follow the information to its source.
